From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shahbaz Youssefi <syoussefi@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 17:04:40 -0400
Subject: Vulkan: Allow staged clears of 3D image slices

Prior to GL_EXT_clear_texture support, only entire levels of 3D images
could be cleared.  The implementation of that extension added
UpdateSource::ClearPartial which allows clearing slices of a 3D image.
As a result, it is no longer necessary to disable deferred clears for
them.

This change is not meant as an optimization however, but a bug fix.  If
a slice of a 3D image is invalidated via the framebuffer and robust-init
is enabled, we automatically attempt to stage a clear to that slice, but
it used to use UpdateSource::Clear which clears the entire level.

Bug: chromium:556750158
Change-Id: I4f2088c9d40f2f22b1b719f997ac9f3cba0f9685
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/angle/angle/+/8446101
Reviewed-by: Charlie Lao <cclao@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Amirali Abdolrashidi <abdolrashidi@google.com>
Commit-Queue: Shahbaz Youssefi <syoussefi@chromium.org>

Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y): vk::LayerIndex/gl::OwnerLayer are
mapped to uint32_t (types absent on this revision), including the new
ImageHelper::clearPartial() signature and the slice-range checks in
flushStagedUpdatesImpl(); new end2end test expectations are dropped
(test-only drift).

